[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 14 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
with a constant-power POWER pump. Three-node topology:

    R1 (suction reservoir, fixed head 5 m)
      |
      +-- PU1 (POWER pump, 7.5 kW) --> J1
                                        |
                                        +-- P1 (pipe) --> J2 (15 L/s consumer)

The dPHM loader translates the POWER row through the conservative
quadratic surrogate fit_power_pump_surrogate(). The surrogate is
anchored on the network's total positive demand (15 L/s) and chooses
a shut-off head of 1.5x the operating head. It is bounded, finite,
and Newton-stable, but it is NOT a faithful constant-power
translation away from the anchor flow. See
docs/epanet-inp-import.md for the exact assumptions and limitations.

SI flow units (LPS), Hazen-Williams head loss. Solvable by
aquaoptima.dphm.newton_solve with jacobian_mode="analytic".

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0     0.0     ;     ; pump discharge node (no consumer)
 J2   0.0    15.0     ;     ; 15 L/s consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1    5.0   ;          ; 5 m fixed-head suction reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   J1      J2      200.0    150.0      130.0       0.0         OPEN

[PUMPS]
;ID    Node1   Node2   Parameters
 PU1   R1      J1      POWER   7.5

[OPTIONS]
 Units                LPS
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
